    "body": "I took out the \"generally restricted\" part because I couldn't describe the nature of the restriction.\r\n\r\nIn Chrome's implementation we're pretty restrictive: we error on anything other than 101, 401 or 407 response, and UI is not shown for authentication or TLS failures. Do you think there's a way we could codify some or all of these restrictions in the standard?",
